# newt-python leak gate — hashed internal-term denylist.
#
# One sha256 hex digest per line, of a lowercased token (or of two adjacent tokens
# joined). scripts/leak_gate.py tokenizes every tracked file and compares digests.
#
# Why hashed: a public file listing our internal terms would be a map of what to grep
# our history for. This is obscurity, not secrecy — short tokens are brute-forceable
# given the digests. The point is that the public repo does not advertise the terms.
#
# Plaintext source + regeneration command live in the private portal repo at
# wiki/operating-docs/leak-gate-terms.txt. Edit there, regenerate, commit both.

